2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=640 640w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=750 750w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=828 828w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1080 1080w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1200 1200w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1440 1440w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1920 1920w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2048 2048w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2400 2400w" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2400"></p></div></div></div></div><section><header><p></p><h2><span>The latest Quick Posts</span></h2><p></p></header><div><div role="article"><div><p><img alt="Terrence O'Brien" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96"></p><p><span>Terrence O'Brien</span><span><time datetime="2026-11-07T17:15:00+00:00">Two hours ago</time></span></p></div><div><p>What classic should Nintendo remake next?</p><p><em><a href="https://www.theverge.com/games/1025415/the-legend-of-zelda-ocarina-of-time-review-nintendo-switch-2">Ocarina of Time</a></em> is one of the most storied installments not just in the Zelda franchise, but in Nintendo history, so it only makes sense that the company would eventually remaster it. Which got us wondering: are there other titles in the Nintendo back catalog that could use a remake — not a sequel — to usher them into the modern console age?</p></div></div><div role="article"><div><p><img alt="Terrence O'Brien" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/02/TERRENCE_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96"></p><p><span>Terrence O'Brien</span><span><time datetime="2026-11-07T14:26:13+00:00">2:26 PM UTC</time></span></p></div><div><p>‘Triplets of Belleville’ director pushes back against AI accusations.</p><p>Sylvain Chomet says no generative AI was used in his <em>Christian Dior’s Night in Color</em> short. Some viewers claim to have spotted glitches and a character with six fingers, but Chomet and producer Aton Soumache say the film was made with traditional 2D animation, and that an automated interpolation tool was used for “a very small part of the process.”</p></div></div><div role="article"><div><p><img alt="Richard Lawler" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/RICHARD_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/RICHARD_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/01/RICHARD_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96"></p><p><span>Richard Lawler</span><span><time datetime="2026-11-06T22:03:37+00:00">Nov 6</time></span></p></div><div><p>TSMC is apparently considering getting into the RAM business at the request of Nvidia.</p><p>A report by <em>The Information</em> claims that the world’s biggest chipmaker is considering adding memory back into its portfolio, starting with <a href="https://www.theverge.com/2011/12/7/2616348/3d-dram-ibm-micron-128-gbps">next-generation 3D DRAM</a>.</p><p>With demand still outpacing supply and prices sky-high, the outlet says it could compete with memory giants Micron, Samsung, and SK Hynix to develop and produce 3D DRAM technology that stacks chips vertically for increased bandwidth, capacity, and power efficiency.</p></div></div></div></section><section><header><p></p><h2><span>Weekend reads</span><span> / </span><span>Catch up on our favorite stories.</span></h2><p></p></header><div><div><p><img alt="Rian Johnson explains why he had to build his own iPhone camera app" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=415 415w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=480 480w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=540 540w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=640 640w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=750 750w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=828 828w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C5.5555555555556%2C100%2C88.888888888889&amp;w=1080 1080w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/Rian-Johnson-Portrait.jpg?quality=90&a