_226036_H_Jang.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=16.691176470588%2C0%2C66.617647058824%2C100&amp;w=2400"></p></div><div><p>Ship of Harkinian is a labor of love years in the making</p><p><span><span><span><span>Derek Hill</span></span></span></span></p></div></div></div></div></section><section><h2>Most Popular</h2><ol><li><p>1</p><div><p><span><span><span><span>Tom Warren</span></span></span></span><span><time datetime="2026-11-05T17:00:00">Nov 5</time></span></p></div></li><li><p>2</p><div><p><span><span><span><span>Andrew Liszewski</span></span></span></span><span><time datetime="2026-11-04T16:36:21">Nov 4</time></span></p></div></li><li><p>3</p><div><p><span><span><span><span>Sean Hollister</span></span></span></span><span><time datetime="2026-11-06T12:00:00">Nov 6</time></span></p></div></li><li><p>4</p><div><p><span><span><span><span>Dominic Preston</span></span></span></span><span><time datetime="2026-11-06T12:30:00">Nov 6</time></span></p></div></li><li><p>5</p><div><p><span><span><span><span>Helen Li</span></span></span></span><span><time datetime="2026-11-06T17:00:00">Nov 6</time></span></p></div></li></ol></section><section><header><p></p><h2><span>In wake of the blue wave</span><span> / </span><span>Following the historic midterms, big changes might be coming for Big Tech.</span></h2><p></p></header><div><div><p><img alt="The fight for tech accountability starts now" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" sizes="100vw" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/10/STK423_ELECTIONS4.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=376 376w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/10/STK423_ELECTIONS4.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=384 384w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/10/STK423_ELECTIONS4.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=415 415w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-co