ontent/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=415 415w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=480 480w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=540 540w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=640 640w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=750 750w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=828 828w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1080 1080w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1200 1200w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1440 1440w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=1920 1920w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2048 2048w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2400 2400w" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/shure-mv7-plus-breakout.png?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=2400"></p><div><p>This Verge-favorite microphone for podcasting is discounted, along with other audio products.</p></div></div><div role="article" id="latest-dmcyOnF1aWNrUG9zdDoxMDI4OTcw"><div><p><img alt="Stevie Bonifield" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" width="34" height="34" decoding="async" data-nimg="1" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/10/STEVIE_BONIFIELD_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=48 1x, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/10/STEVIE_BONIFIELD_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96 2x" src="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2025/10/STEVIE_BONIFIELD_BLURPLE.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=96"></p><p><span>Stevie Bonifield</span><span><time datetime="2026-11-06T19:13:42+00:00">Nov 6</time></span></p></div><div><p>OpenAI says it found 948 local privilege escalation vulnerabilities in the Linux kernel.</p><p>It says it used an upcoming cyber model to autonomously <a href="https://openai.com/index/a-thousand-fewer-paths-to-root/" rel="noopener">scan the latest Linux kernel</a> as of “mid-October 2026.” OpenAI’s system also generated patches for the bugs, and it says a human researcher reviewed them.</p></div></div><div id="latest-dmcyOnBvc3Q6MTAyODIyOA=="><p><img alt="Lame-duck Congress might actually do something: speed up energy projects" data-chromatic="ignore" loading="lazy" decoding="async" data-nimg="fill" sizes="(max-width: 768px) 100vw, (max-width: 1180px) 50vw, 640px" srcset="https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.jpg?quality=90&amp;strip=all&amp;crop=0%2C0%2C100%2C100&amp;w=256 256w, https://platform.theverge.com/wp-content/uploads/sites/2/2026/11/268857_cutting_red_tape_to_build_more_powerlines__CVirginia-1.